From cffc8accc67d3593682dfed9a512b679c8c174fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knfsd-fuzz <knfsd-fuzz@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tools/execprog: raise the program budget for long upcall
 waits

The per-program budget is 5s scaled by min(slowdown, 3), so no
slowdown lets a program wait out a 30s kernel upcall timeout: the fork
server kills it and aborts its remote coverage generation.

Add rpcserver.Config.ProgramTimeout, which raises the budget sent to the
executor, and syz-execprog -program-timeout to set it.  A budget that
the default already covers or that reaches the no-output timeout is
rejected.  Record unfinished calls in the coverage .meta so a program
stopped at its budget is distinguishable from one whose generation
published no remote coverage.
---
